2.
Definitions.
- In these rules, unless the context otherwise requires,-
(a)
"Act" means the Right to Information Act, 2005 (
22 of 2005
);
(b)
"Commission" means the Central Information Commission constituted under sub-section (1) of Section 12 of the Act;
(c)
"First Appellate Authority" means an officer in the public authority who is senior in rank to the Central Public Information
Officer to whom an appeal under sub-section (1) of Section 19 of the Act lies;
(d)
"Registrar" means an officer of the Commission so designated and includes an Additional Registrar, Joint Registrar and
Deputy Registrar;
(e)
"Section" means a Section of the Act;
(f)
all other words and expressions used herein but not defined in these rules shall have the same meanings assigned to
them in the Act.
